00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:01.290
There are some Adventurers who went missing.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:05.200
There've been rumors about it
since right after the Apocalypse, though.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.040
A mere coincidence... They just parted
from their comrades for some reason.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.200
That's one theory people have.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:16.620
Another one is that it was
similar to Krusty's case.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:19.410
Where the heck did you go, Lycopene?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.880
"Missing Person"

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:25.240
If I remember correctly, your friend, too...

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.080
I became convinced about it

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.540
because I could no longer get
in touch with my friend Oshima.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.990
The names of the Adventurers in your friend list

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:40.120
will never disappear as long
as they're within the same server.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:41.230
Pon-Pon Taro

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:41.230
TAMA-yan

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:41.230
Oshima

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:41.700
And yet...

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:45.870
We've also confirmed they're
not in any of the other servers.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:49.620
Shiroe. Do you really think...

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:54.790
...that they've returned to the Earth in reality?

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.660
Yes, though that may be
wishful thinking on my part.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:04.660
However... to return, I believe that
the Adventurers needed to agree to it.

