00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:04.630
{=7}Top Secret

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.260
Summoner Genius - Taricton
Rank: Raid

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:09.950
Taricton, the Summoner Genius said,

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.080
"Those who agree to offer up
their souls shall accept access

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.830
and select standby mode in their sleep."

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.620
Of course, I don't know if they returned safely.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:27.830
So in order to confirm it,
we need to go there and come back here,

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:30.040
instead of returning there.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:36.200
Things are becoming more complicated.
Well, I'll just leave it to you guys.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:41.870
More importantly... don't you think
Eins might become a problem soon?

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:46.410
He seems to be connected to Plant Hwyaden, too.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:51.410
Minami, the second
largest player city in Yamato...

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.830
Plant hwyaden, the only
guild there, controls the city

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.410
Intix - Elf - Sorcerer

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.830
and is connected to the Holy Empire Westelande.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.270
KR - Elf - Summoner

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:03.740
And Westelande has hostile relations

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:08.450
with the League of Freedom Cities Eastal
ruled by the Cowen Family.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:13.870
So there's a risk that we Adventurers
might get dragged into their conflict.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.870
There are loads of problems, huh?

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:22.200
It seems better to resolve issues close to us.

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.450
Here's some chocolatey latte.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:27.550
Chocolatey Latte

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.790
Our power of femininity will go up.

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:33.490
Hmm... Power of femininity, huh?

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.490
This is delicious.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:38.540
Did you get scolded
by that lady in the carriage?

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:39.740
What?

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:43.080
I saw her in town. Did she bring some news?

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:47.740
Your forehead showed distress,
just like my lord's.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.370
My forehead did?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:54.580
To tell you the truth,
my mother paid a visit, and... um...

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:58.740
My... marriage has been decided.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:02.950
I don't know how much
longer I can stay in Akiba.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.830
Why don't you turn it down?

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:07.950
I cannot do that.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.540
Why not?

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:13.910
That's how I've been taught since my childhood.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:19.240
Um... You don't have to look so sad.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:22.080
This is... quite normal.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:25.240
You're the one who looks troubled, Rayneshia.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:29.620
I look like that? I... see...

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:36.240
I thought you were going
to date that scary four-eyes.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.080
You mean Sir Krusty?! No way!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.580
You did seem concerned about him, so...

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:45.790
That's because... he's a Guardian Knight.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:53.290
Guardian Knights act as protectors.
So in a way, it means he protects me.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:58.290
But it's not against the rules to be in love
with your Guardian Knight, right?

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:04.330
Wh-What about you, Akatsuki?
You're dating a scary four-eyes, too.

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:09.120
M-My lord isn't scary at all.

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:14.080
He's kind and lets me ride
on a Griffon with him.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:20.330
A-And, I'm not dating him.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:25.200
To think that my Guardian Knight
is absent at a time like this...

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.200
I'm getting a little upset.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.620
There'll probably be a rescue operation.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:32.540
That's not necessary.

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:37.830
I bet he's spending a carefree time
with a straight face right now.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:39.660
If not...

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:49.120
If not, he probably looks like he dropped
everything and disappeared from battle,

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:54.620
thinking that he doesn't care.
I bet that's how that monster four-eyes looks.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.660
It's a little disappointing...

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.160
that I can't slap him for that.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:07.370
Job satisfaction?

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:10.290
In order to help them,
we should create a new business

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:13.910
with irrigation or river improvement
to promote employment.

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:16.160
Like we said, there isn't money.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.990
We can collect it.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:20.830
Both Shopping Street 8 and Marine Agency

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:24.830
must have a large amount of assets.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:30.040
Our guild is big, but I don't want
you to think we have a lot of money.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:33.580
Our guild is poor.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:41.830
I heard Shopping Street 8 built a
new trading establishment in Maihama.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:46.370
That alone must've required
over 1.5 million golds of investment.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:52.450
Oh, that building isn't under
Shopping Street 8's name.

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:56.290
It's under the Maihama Trading Facility
Management Committee's name.

00:17:56.290 --> 00:18:00.910
The money to build the facility
was gathered from guild members

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:04.700
by dividing the rights to use the storage
and the shop space in advance.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:10.790
So the members who didn't invest
will pay a higher price for the rights.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:16.620
Anyway, it's not Shopping Street 8's asset,
so we're not making any money.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:18.450
I see.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.540
So that's how it was built, huh?

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.620
I don't get it at all.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.290
Don't worry, Isaac.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.950
Neither do I.

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.740
I'll have Shiro explain it to me later.

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:34.490
Being able to use that kind
of scheme proves your guild has power.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:39.700
Leading trading guilds should be more
considerate to average Adventurers.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:46.450
Well, the leader of the Management
Committee is a little over level 50.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:50.370
He's afraid of battles and
doesn't have any crafting subclass,

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:55.620
so he started a project that consists of
only making courtesy visits and admin work.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:59.200
Well... Isn't that incredible?

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.790
That's...

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:06.580
Why don't you guys do
that kind of work too, Eins?

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:11.080
Eins.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:18.240
It's not like we don't want to support them.
In fact, we do support them.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.870
The Adventurers registered
at the adventure placement office

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.620
are now all above level 50.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:29.240
That's the number we aimed for when
Krusty was around at the beginning.

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:32.120
And Mr. Krusty isn't here now.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:35.950
Doesn't it mean this is dysfunctional?

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:39.830
What meaning does this place hold
when various decisions can't be made?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.660
Hey! What do you mean by that?

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.580
The leader is absent.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:47.830
When the Round Table Conference
cannot display leadership,

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.490
is it worthy of existence?

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:56.490
Eins!

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.870
The Round Table Conference is autonomous,

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.870
but it's not a governing organization

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:05.370
and its activities are based
on the participants' goodwill.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:08.240
We're supposed to be here
to carry out the intent of

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:13.410
all the Adventurers in this town
as well as the People of the Land.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:17.740
Krusty is our representative,
but he's not a President.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:22.830
And the fact that he's not
around doesn't change our mission.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:29.540
Then this Conference is...

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:36.830
The Round Table Conference doesn't
have the power of compurrsion.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:39.870
Only when all the purrticipating guilds agree

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:44.080
do all the purrojects get carried out.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:49.450
Eins probably held out hope that
a higher power, Krusty, for example,

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:53.700
would approve of his opinion.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:57.330
But even that was denied.

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:00.410
Even if milord agrees,

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:06.160
if the Round Table Conference doesn't agree,
the opinion doesn't get passed.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.790
Understood.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:16.040
Then Honesty will seek our own path.

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:24.660
Good work, Shiroechi.

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:27.160
Thanks, Chief.

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:30.450
But it's not like everything
was resolved, right?

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.120
Oh? You look down, Shiroe.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:35.620
Wanna see my panties?

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:36.910
I'll slice you.

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:41.330
Things weren't resolved, but yeah...

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:44.370
I think we bought some time.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:53.910
If I remember correctly, that's...
the crest of the Holy Empire Westelande.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.830
And that one is... the Saiguu Family's?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:00.160
There's trouble, Shiroe!

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.080
Eins became a fluke!

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:04.160
There, there. Akatsuki!

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:05.910
This is insufferable.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:07.200
What's going on?

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:10.950
I heard that Westelande
officially appointed Eins...

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:11.390
What?

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:14.330
As a fluke! A drake! No, no...!

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:15.540
Huh?

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:18.230
Duke

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:17.540
A duke, you mean?

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:18.700
That's it!

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:21.740
He was appointed as a duke in Akiba?!

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:23.870
What does that mean, my lord?

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.740
The Round Table Conference is...

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:30.450
The town of Akiba is... going to fall apart!

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:32.620
So this is the path Honesty chose?

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:37.700
This is what you chose, Eins?!

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:15.290
The Saiguu Family stands at the top
of the People of the Land in Yamato.

00:24:15.290 --> 00:24:17.660
Their messenger pays a visit to Rayneshia.

00:24:17.660 --> 00:24:20.740
The preparation for her marriage moves forward,
whether she's ready or not.

00:24:20.740 --> 00:24:23.910
Meanwhile, receiving the title of Duke,
Eins declares his intention

00:24:23.910 --> 00:24:26.330
to part from Shiroe and the others.

00:24:26.330 --> 00:24:30.330
The Round Table Conference
at last begins to collapse.

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:36.990
Next Time

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:36.990
The Duke of Akiba

00:24:30.330 --> 00:24:32.620
Next Time: "The Duke of Akiba."

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:35.200
When things go past
the breaking point, rules change.
